meta {
  name: RunTurn — the agent acts
  type: grpc
  seq: 1
}

grpc {
  url: {{coreGrpc}}
  method: /dop.v1.AgentService/RunTurn
  body: grpc
  auth: none
}

metadata {
  x-actor-id: {{actorId}}
  x-account-id: {{accountId}}
  x-request-id: {{$guid}}
}

body:grpc {
  [
    {
      "demand_id": "{{demandId}}",
      "thread_id": "{{threadId}}",
      "text": "why is the orders query slow?",
      "task_kind": "investigation",
      "resource_id": "{{agentResourceId}}",
      "idempotency_key": "{{$guid}}"
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  One turn of the agent. The runtime lives in the CORE (ADR-0023): the provider's
  credential leaves the vault and is used in the same process, without crossing the
  network.

  An empty `resource_id` uses the account's only integration of category `agent`;
  with more than one, the core REFUSES with the list instead of choosing.

  **The idempotency key is mandatory and the edge does not invent one:** a turn
  spends money, and a generated key would turn a network retry into double
  consumption.

  With a provisioned sandbox, the agent ACTS — the tool loop runs a command inside
  the demand's isolated environment, with a ceiling of 8 rounds and consumption
  recorded on each one.
}
